/* book Worked example 2: Q: The same channel is equalized adaptively by LMS in training mode with μ = 0.1 and starting taps (c−1, c0, c1) = (0, 1, 0). The training symbols are a(0) … a(5) = +1, +1, −1, +1, +1, −1 and there is no noise. Do the updates at n = 2 and n = 3.
   1. Received samples x(n) = 0.2a(n+1) + a(n) + 0.3a(n−1): x(1) = 1.1, x(2) = −0.5, x(3) = 0.9, x(4) = 1.1.
   2. n = 2: taps hold (x(3), x(2), x(1)) = (0.9, −0.5, 1.1). y = 0(0.9) + 1(−0.5) + 0(1.1) = −0.5. d = a(2) = −1, so e = −1 − (−0.5) = −0.5.
   3. Update: c = (0, 1, 0) + 0.1 × (−0.5) × (0.9, −0.5, 1.1) = (−0.045, 1.025, −0.055).
   4. n = 3: taps hold (x(4), x(3), x(2)) = (1.1, 0.9, −0.5). y = −0.045(1.1) + 1.025(0.9) − 0.055(−0.5) = 0.9005. d = a(3) = +1, so e = 0.0995.
   5. Update: c = (−0.045, 1.025, −0.055) + 0.00995 × (1.1, 0.9, −0.5) = (−0.0341, 1.0340, −0.0600).
   6. The squared error fell from 0.25 to 0.0099, and every tap has moved towards the zero-forcing signs (negative, above 1, negative).
   Answer: After two updates c = (−0.0341, 1.0340, −0.0600); the errors were −0.5 and 0.0995. */
